{"id": 26, "ts": 1780483074.301468, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m afraid I don\u2019t have any concrete observations of Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation or his leadership style in the cockpit. The notes I have focus on his technical strengths \u2013 he responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, and takes responsibility seriously \u2013 but they also flag him as \u201cmoody\u201d and a \u201cloner.\u201d Those personality cues raise a reasonable doubt about how smoothly he would integrate into a multi\u2011crew environment, especially on long\u2011haul flights where sustained interpersonal coordination is vital.\nGiven that gap, and weighing the evidence we do have, I still see Candidate\u202fB as the strongest overall fit. B\u2019s conscientiousness supports operational reliability; his proven stress resilience and solid weather\u2011assessment and computer skills address technical competence; and while his pretentious tone is a concern, it appears more manageable through crew\u2011resource\u2011management training than the fundamental uncertainty we have around D\u2019s ability to cooperate and lead. Therefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fB."}
